Vitamin D helps regulate the amount of calcium and phosphate in the body (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/vitamin-d).  
It is found in foods such as oily fish, egg yolks and fortified spreads (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/bone-health/food-for-strong-bones).  
The recommended daily intake for adults and children over 4 is 10 micrograms throughout the year (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-d).  

