Melatonin is a natural hormone produced by the pineal gland that helps control the sleep cycle (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/melatonin/about-melatonin). The maximum recommended dose is 10 mg taken once daily (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/melatonin/how-and-when-to-take-melatonin). Melatonin is available only on prescription and is not authorised for sale as a supplement in the UK (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/melatonin/about-melatonin).

